IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aoma-majority`

-- Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as
-- parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The Act puts no duty on anyone and names no official. It fixes, "for all the purposes of the laws of the
-- State", the moment a person reaches an age (s 4) and the line of full age and full capacity at 18 (s 5(1)), and how
-- words like "minor", "infant", "adult" and "full age" in other WA laws and documents are read (s 5(2)-(7)). Two kinds
-- of person ask it questions:
--   - the young person, about their own age: the baseline's seat (aoma-majority.l4);
--   - a parent, guardian, trustee, executor or anyone else dealing with a young person (a party to a contract with
--     them, an employer), about that young person's age: the same rules, asked about someone else, with answers worded
--     in the third person.
-- "How is a word like 'minor' or 'adult' read in this law or document" is the same question for both, so it is asked
-- of both roles.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and answers `does not arise for you` when the
-- situation does not hold, without reading anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, with the
-- same name, type and @desc, so the form asks it once. There are two:
--   - `a law or document I am asking about uses a word like "minor" or "adult"` (BOOLEAN): the s 5(2) question arises
--     only when a WA law, a will, a contract, a trust deed or another document uses such a word, or an age in years.
--     FALSE: does not arise. Taken by the one word question, for both roles.
--   - `someone is said to lack the legal capacity to do something` (BOOLEAN): the s 5(4) question, whether coming of
--     full age removes an incapacity, arises only when there is an incapacity to ask about. FALSE: does not arise.
--     Taken by the two incapacity questions, one per role.
-- The questions of s 4 and s 5(1) (when an age is reached, when full age comes, whether one is an adult on a day)
-- arise for every person of each role, so they take no situation input.
--
-- The rules are in aoma-majority.l4. This module calls them and restates none. For the young person each answer is the
-- baseline export's own answer, wrapped (`the answer is`). For the other role, the baseline's first-person answers are
-- reworded in the third person, value for value. No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am the young person, asking about my own age`
    `I am a parent, guardian, trustee or other person dealing with a young person`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

-- The young person's answers: the baseline's own answer types, with `does not arise for you`.
DECLARE `When I reach an age, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `When I reach the age`

DECLARE `When I come of full age, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `When I come of full age`

DECLARE `Whether I am an adult in law, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS AN `Am I an adult in law`

-- Both roles: how the word is read (the baseline's answers are not worded from a seat).
DECLARE `How the word is read, if it arises` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the answer is` HAS `the answer` IS A `How the expression is read`

-- The other role's answers: the baseline's answers, value for value, in the third person.
DECLARE `When the young person reaches an age` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `from the very start of` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `not fixed by s 4: the anniversary fell before the commencing day`
    `not fixed by the Act: the young person was born on 29 February and that year has no 29 February`

DECLARE `When the young person comes of full age` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `on turning 18, from the very start of` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `on the commencing day, which was` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `not decided by this Act: the person was 21 or over on the commencing day`
    `not decided by this Act: the young person was born on 29 February and their 18th year has no 29 February`

DECLARE `Whether the young person is an adult in law` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `yes: of full age and full capacity under s 5(1)(a)`
    `yes: of full age and full capacity under s 5(1)(b)`
    `not yet: the young person is not of full age on that day`
    `not decided by this Act: the person was 21 or over on the commencing day`
    `not decided by this Act: the young person was born on 29 February and their 18th year has no 29 February`

-- The cause of the young person's incapacity, worded for the other role; the baseline's `my age` is `their age`.
DECLARE `What the young person's incapacity is due to` IS ONE OF
    `their age`
    `insanity`
    `mental infirmity`
    `another factor distinct from age`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The rewordings list every value and have no OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31: a CONSIDER with OTHERWISE takes the
-- OTHERWISE branch for an ASSUMEd value instead of failing, so a case could not show the value was not read).
GIVEN `the answer` IS A `When I reach the age`
GIVETH A `When the young person reaches an age`
`in the third person, the age answer` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `at the very start of` d THEN `from the very start of` d
    WHEN `not fixed by s 4: the anniversary fell before the commencing day` THEN `not fixed by s 4: the anniversary fell before the commencing day`
    WHEN `not fixed by the Act: I was born on 29 February and that year has no 29 February` THEN `not fixed by the Act: the young person was born on 29 February and that year has no 29 February`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `When I come of full age`
GIVETH A `When the young person comes of full age`
`in the third person, the full age answer` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `on attaining 18, at the very start of` d THEN `on turning 18, from the very start of` d
    WHEN `on the commencing day` d THEN `on the commencing day, which was` d
    WHEN `not decided by this Act: I was 21 or over on the commencing day` THEN `not decided by this Act: the person was 21 or over on the commencing day`
    WHEN `not decided by this Act: I was born on 29 February and my 18th year has no 29 February` THEN `not decided by this Act: the young person was born on 29 February and their 18th year has no 29 February`

GIVEN `the answer` IS AN `Am I an adult in law`
GIVETH A `Whether the young person is an adult in law`
`in the third person, the adult answer` `the answer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer`
    WHEN `yes: of full age and full capacity under s 5(1)(a)` THEN `yes: of full age and full capacity under s 5(1)(a)`
    WHEN `yes: of full age and full capacity under s 5(1)(b)` THEN `yes: of full age and full capacity under s 5(1)(b)`
    WHEN `not yet: I am not of full age on that day` THEN `not yet: the young person is not of full age on that day`
    WHEN `not decided by this Act: I was 21 or over on the commencing day` THEN `not decided by this Act: the person was 21 or over on the commencing day`
    WHEN `not decided by this Act: I was born on 29 February and my 18th year has no 29 February` THEN `not decided by this Act: the young person was born on 29 February and their 18th year has no 29 February`

GIVEN `the cause` IS A `What the young person's incapacity is due to`
GIVETH A `The cause of the incapacity`
`the baseline's cause for` `the cause` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the cause`
    WHEN `their age` THEN `my age`
    WHEN `insanity` THEN `insanity`
    WHEN `mental infirmity` THEN `mental infirmity`
    WHEN `another factor distinct from age` THEN `another factor distinct from age`

§§ `For the young person, asking about my own age (ss 4, 5)`

§§§ `s 4 -- the moment I reach an age`

@export When, in law, do I reach a given age (Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA) s 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the age` IS A NUMBER @desc The age in years you are asking about, for example 18
      `the commencing day` IS A DATE @desc The day the Age of Majority Act 1972 came into operation, fixed by proclamation under s 2 (not in the deposited text), ISO 8601
GIVETH A `When I reach an age, if it arises`
`When in law do I reach an age` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the young person, asking about my own age` THEN `the answer is` (`When do I reach this age` `my date of birth` `the age` `the commencing day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 5(1) -- when I come of full age and full capacity`

@export When do I come of full age and full capacity (Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA) s 5(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the commencing day` IS A DATE @desc The day the Age of Majority Act 1972 came into operation, fixed by proclamation under s 2 (not in the deposited text), ISO 8601
GIVETH A `When I come of full age, if it arises`
`When do I come of full age and full capacity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the young person, asking about my own age` THEN `the answer is` (`When do I come of full age` `my date of birth` `the commencing day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I an adult in law (of full age and full capacity) on a given day (Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA) s 5(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about, ISO 8601
      `the commencing day` IS A DATE @desc The day the Age of Majority Act 1972 came into operation, fixed by proclamation under s 2 (not in the deposited text), ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Whether I am an adult in law, if it arises`
`Am I an adult in law on the day I ask about` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the young person, asking about my own age` THEN `the answer is` (`Am I an adult in law on this day` `my date of birth` `the day asked about` `the commencing day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 5(4) -- what coming of full age does not cure`

@export Does coming of full age at 18 remove this incapacity of mine (Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA) s 5(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `someone is said to lack the legal capacity to do something` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, or the young person you are asking about, are said to lack the legal capacity to do something (for example to make a binding contract or a will)
      `the cause` IS A `The cause of the incapacity` @desc What the lack of legal capacity is due to
      `I have attained full age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have come of full age under s 5(1)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my coming of full age remove this incapacity of mine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the young person, asking about my own age` THEN
        IF NOT (`someone is said to lack the legal capacity to do something`)
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does turning 18 remove this incapacity` `the cause` `I have attained full age`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a parent, guardian, trustee or other person dealing with a young person (ss 4, 5)`

§§§ `s 4 -- the moment the young person reaches an age`

@export When, in law, does the young person reach a given age, for example an age a will or trust names (Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA) s 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the young person's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The young person's date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the age` IS A NUMBER @desc The age in years you are asking about, for example 18
      `the commencing day` IS A DATE @desc The day the Age of Majority Act 1972 came into operation, fixed by proclamation under s 2 (not in the deposited text), ISO 8601
GIVETH A `When the young person reaches an age`
`When in law does the young person reach an age` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent, guardian, trustee or other person dealing with a young person` THEN `in the third person, the age answer` (`When do I reach this age` `the young person's date of birth` `the age` `the commencing day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 5(1) -- when the young person comes of full age and full capacity`

@export When does the young person come of full age and full capacity (Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA) s 5(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the young person's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The young person's date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the commencing day` IS A DATE @desc The day the Age of Majority Act 1972 came into operation, fixed by proclamation under s 2 (not in the deposited text), ISO 8601
GIVETH A `When the young person comes of full age`
`When does the young person come of full age and full capacity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent, guardian, trustee or other person dealing with a young person` THEN `in the third person, the full age answer` (`When do I come of full age` `the young person's date of birth` `the commencing day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is the young person an adult in law (of full age and full capacity) on a given day, for example the day a contract with them is made (Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA) s 5(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the young person's date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The young person's date of birth, ISO 8601
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about, ISO 8601
      `the commencing day` IS A DATE @desc The day the Age of Majority Act 1972 came into operation, fixed by proclamation under s 2 (not in the deposited text), ISO 8601
GIVETH A `Whether the young person is an adult in law`
`Is the young person an adult in law on the day I ask about` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent, guardian, trustee or other person dealing with a young person` THEN `in the third person, the adult answer` (`Am I an adult in law on this day` `the young person's date of birth` `the day asked about` `the commencing day`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 5(4) -- what coming of full age does not cure`

@export Does the young person's coming of full age at 18 remove this incapacity of theirs (Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA) s 5(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `someone is said to lack the legal capacity to do something` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, or the young person you are asking about, are said to lack the legal capacity to do something (for example to make a binding contract or a will)
      `the cause of their incapacity` IS A `What the young person's incapacity is due to` @desc What the young person's lack of legal capacity is due to
      `the young person has attained full age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the young person has come of full age under s 5(1)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does the young person's coming of full age remove this incapacity of theirs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a parent, guardian, trustee or other person dealing with a young person` THEN
        IF NOT (`someone is said to lack the legal capacity to do something`)
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Does turning 18 remove this incapacity` (`the baseline's cause for` `the cause of their incapacity`) `the young person has attained full age`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For everyone: a word like "minor" or "adult" in another law or document (s 5(2), (3), (5), (7))`

§§§ `s 5(2), (3), (5), (7) -- how the word is read`

@export How is a word like "minor", "infant", "adult" or "full age" read in this law or document: does it mean the line of 18 (Age of Majority Act 1972 (WA) s 5(2), (3), (5), (7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a law or document I am asking about uses a word like "minor" or "adult"` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a law, a will, a contract, a trust deed or another document you are asking about uses a word like "minor", "infant", "adult", "full age" or "majority", or an age in years
      `the expression` IS A `The expression` @desc The word or phrase used in the other law or document
      `the place` IS A `Where the expression appears` @desc The kind of law or document it appears in
      `it has its own definition or a contrary intention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that law or document defines the word itself, or shows it means something else
GIVETH A `How the word is read, if it arises`
`How is a word like minor or adult read in this law or document` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am the young person, asking about my own age` THEN
        IF NOT (`a law or document I am asking about uses a word like "minor" or "adult"`)
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` (`How is this expression read` `the expression` `the place` `it has its own definition or a contrary intention`)
    WHEN `I am a parent, guardian, trustee or other person dealing with a young person` THEN
        IF NOT (`a law or document I am asking about uses a word like "minor" or "adult"`)
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the answer is` (`How is this expression read` `the expression` `the place` `it has its own definition or a contrary intention`)
